  "why": "The Elusive Samurai second season, a 12 episode summer 2026 TV run airing 2026-07-17 to 2026-10-02 and still on air at labelling time. AniZip 18903 is the same run: SAME_AS ids to mal:60059 and anilist:182616, the same episodeCount of 12, and a first episode dated 2026-07-17, the run's own start date. The Crunchyroll season GQWH0M19X-GS00366034 is the same run: it maps SAME_AS onto all four members, and although it numbers its episodes 13 to 21 continuing on from the first season, those nine fall on exactly the AniZip dates 2026-07-17 through 2026-09-11 with the same titles, so it is the aired part of this cour rather than a wider season (nine is fewer than twelve). The bare Crunchyroll series GQWH0M19X has no dates, count or episodes of its own, and Kitsu records it as a PART_OF container for this run, so it holds the run. AniZip episodes 1 to 9 pair with Crunchyroll 13 to 21 on identical release days and matching titles, from Longing for Sea Bream! to The Man Called Masashige Kusunoki, which is also what fixes the offset of twelve between the two numberings. Kitsu's episodes 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 and 7 pair with the same AniZip positions on exact titles (Ayako's Heart-Pounding Operation!, The Warrior of Love: Shinano Mask!, The Unyielding, The Boy Who Became a God, My Uncle, and Longing for a Sea Bream! which differs from AniZip only by an article). Kitsu episode 3 is titled Tokiyuki and the Three Generals where AniZip and Crunchyroll both have Tokiyuki and Three Great Generals, and Kitsu carries no dates, so that position is left unpaired, as are Kitsu's untitled episodes 8 to 12 and AniZip's untitled episodes 10, 11 and 12."
